    <bpmn:process id="W_W1325" name="W1325. Employee Death-in-Service Benefits Processing &amp; Beneficiary Claim Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Notification of employee death (from family, supervisor, or workplace incident report per W140)
Frequency: Estimated 3–5 employee deaths per year across 6,918 employees (based on Philippine actuarial mortality rates for working-age population)
Volume: 1 beneficiary claim per event; processing time-sensitive due to family&#x27;s financial need
Owner: HR Head (CHRO)
Participants: HR Head, HR Assistant, Payroll Officer, Finance, VP Legal, Insurance Coordinator, Department Head/Store Manager, Deceased Employee&#x27;s Beneficiary/Family, SSS, Pag-IBIG, HMO Provider
Source: workflow W1325 — Employee Death-in-Service Benefits Processing &amp; Beneficiary Claim Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1325_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1325_Lane1" name="HR Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1325_Lane2" name="HR Assistant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1325_Lane3" name="Payroll Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1325_Lane4" name="Insurance Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1325_Lane5" name="HR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1325_End18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1325_Start7" name="Notification of employee death (from family, supervisor, or workplace incident report per…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task8" name="Death notification &amp; immediate response">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Death notification &amp; immediate response: HR receives notification of employee death: (a) if workplace death: Store Manager/DC Supervisor activates emergency response per W140 and W238; COO and VP Legal notified immediately; DOLE notified within 48 hours per W140 reporting requirements; (b) if non-workplace death: Department Head or family notifies HR; (c) HR Head activates death-in-service protocol: (i) HR Assistant creates deceased employee record with death date, cause (if known), and beneficiary information from employee master; (ii) system immediately freezes employee&#x27;s payroll, system access (per W43.5), and company credit cards/accounts; (iii) HR Head contacts Department Head/Store Manager to arrange: (a) company condolence visit to family, (b) funeral assistance (typically PHP 20,000–50,000 from company fund per W489), (c) leave coverage for team members attending wake/funeral; (iv) HR Head assigns dedicated HR Assistant as single point of contact for the family throughout the process
Responsible (R): HR Head / HR Assistant
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task9" name="Beneficiary identification &amp; documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Beneficiary identification &amp; documentation: HR Assistant contacts family to identify and verify beneficiaries: (a) primary beneficiary: spouse and/or children (per SSS rules — legitimate, illegitimate, or legally adopted); (b) secondary beneficiary: parents (if no primary beneficiary); (c) designated beneficiaries: check employee master for any designated beneficiaries on file (life insurance, retirement fund, Pag-IBIG); (d) required documents from family: (i) death certificate (PSA-certified), (ii) marriage certificate (if spouse claiming), (iii) birth certificates of children (if children claiming), (iv) valid IDs of all claimants, (v) funeral receipts for reimbursement; (e) HR Assistant assists family in obtaining documents if needed; (f) HR records all beneficiary information and document receipt in system
Responsible (R): HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: 1–2 weeks (document collection)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task10" name="Final pay computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Final pay computation: Payroll Officer computes final pay per W43.10: (a) pro-rated salary through date of death; (b) pro-rated 13th month pay (1/12 × months worked); (c) unused VL monetization per company policy; (d) less: any outstanding loans or cash advances (company policy may waive deductions upon death as compassionate gesture); (e) final pay released to designated beneficiary within 5 business days per BuildRight policy (faster than standard W43 timeline given family&#x27;s financial need); (f) tax treatment: final pay (salary + 13th month + VL conversion) taxed per normal payroll rules; separation pay due to death is tax-exempt per NIRC Section 32(B)(6)(b)
Responsible (R): Payroll Officer
Accountable (A): Payroll Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task11" name="SSS death benefit processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: SSS death benefit processing: HR Assistant assists family in filing SSS death benefit claim: (a) SSS death benefit: monthly pension for primary beneficiaries (spouse + children &lt; 21 years old) or lump sum for secondary beneficiaries (parents); amount based on employee&#x27;s SSS contribution history and CYS (credited years of service); (b) SSS funeral benefit: PHP 20,000–40,000 (one-time) to whoever paid for funeral expenses; (c) HR provides: (i) SSS contribution history printout, (ii) employer certification of employment and compensation, (iii) certified true copy of death certificate, (iv) other SSS-required forms (DDR, DDRF, DDRS); (d) HR Assistant assists family in filing at nearest SSS branch; processing time: 2–6 months from filing to first pension payment; (e) if work-related death: SSS/ECC Employees&#x27; Compensation (EC) death benefit: additional monthly pension + PHP 30,000 funeral benefit; filed separately per W805 workers&#x27; compensation process
Responsible (R): HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: 3–5 hours (preparation) + 2–6 months SSS processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task12" name="Pag-IBIG death benefit processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Pag-IBIG death benefit processing: HR Assistant assists family in filing Pag-IBIG death and disability claim (DTD): (a) Pag-IBIG death benefit: PHP 20,000–80,000 (one-time) depending on membership duration and total accumulated savings (TAV); (b) Pag-IBIG savings withdrawal: deceased member&#x27;s total accumulated savings (employee + employer contributions + dividends) withdrawn by beneficiaries; (c) HR provides employer certification and contribution history; (d) filed at nearest Pag-IBIG branch; processing time: 1–3 months
Responsible (R): HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: 2–3 hours (preparation) + 1–3 months processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task13" name="Company life insurance claim">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Company life insurance claim: Insurance Coordinator processes group life insurance claim per W863: (a) verify employee&#x27;s coverage under BuildRight&#x27;s group life insurance policy (coverage amount: typically 1–2× annual basic salary); (b) submit claim to insurance provider: death certificate, completed claim form, employer certification; (c) insurance company processes claim: 2–4 weeks for natural death; 4–8 weeks for accidental death (requires investigation); (d) benefit paid to designated beneficiary (not necessarily SSS/Pag-IBIG beneficiary — employee may have designated different person); (e) if work-related death: additional coverage under workers&#x27; compensation insurance per W805/W861
Responsible (R): Insurance Coordinator
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours (preparation) + 2–8 weeks processing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task14" name="Retirement fund benefit (if vested)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Retirement fund benefit (if vested): If deceased employee was vested in BuildRight&#x27;s retirement fund per W977: (a) HR computes vested retirement benefit: employee&#x27;s accumulated company contributions + earnings; (b) retirement fund benefit paid to designated beneficiary; (c) tax-exempt per BIR rules (retirement/death benefit); (d) Finance processes from retirement fund account
Responsible (R): HR / Finance
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task15" name="PhilHealth medical expense reimbursement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: PhilHealth medical expense reimbursement: If deceased employee had outstanding medical bills prior to death: (a) HR assists family in filing PhilHealth reimbursement for hospitalization expenses within 60 days of discharge; (b) PhilHealth deductions from final hospital bill reduce family&#x27;s out-of-pocket medical costs
Responsible (R): HR Assistant
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1325_Task16" name="System closure &amp; record retention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: System closure &amp; record retention: HR completes administrative closure: (a) system updates employee status to &quot;Separated — Deceased&quot;; (b) deactivates all system access per W43.5; (c) removes from active payroll per W43.12; (d) files all death benefit documentation in employee&#x27;s permanent record; (e) retains record for 10 years per BIR and SSS requirements; (f) updates HR analytics: death-in-service statistics feed into workforce planning and insurance renewal data per W863
Responsible (R): HR Assistant / System
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1325_Task17" name="Post-processing follow-up">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Post-processing follow-up: HR Assistant follows up with family on outstanding claims: (a) SSS pension approval status (2–6 month processing); (b) Pag-IBIG claim status (1–3 months); (c) any insurance claim delays; (d) HR Assistant available for 6 months post-death to assist with government agency follow-ups; (e) for workplace deaths: VP Legal monitors DOLE investigation per W140 and any potential criminal liability per RA 11058 (OSH Law)
Responsible (R): HR Assistant
Accountable (A): HR Head
Duration: ~2 hours/month for 6 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1325_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1325_End18" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1325_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1325_Annotation19">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-300 (ensure controlled execution — Separation &amp; Benefits (PA-19.5).) | - operational: BuildRight&#x27;s compassionate advance: company may advance PHP 50,000–100,000 to the family (interest-free, recoverable from SSS/Pag-IBIG proceeds) per CFO authorization; operational: rotating assignments and offering counseling support per W51 employee wellness programs; operational: annual beneficiary confirmation as part of benefits enrollment per W251
Owner: HR Head (CHRO)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1325_Assoc20" sourceRef="W1325_Annotation19" targetRef="W1325_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
