    <bpmn:process id="W_W1385" name="W1385. Employee Separation Pay Computation, DOLE Clearance &amp; Retirement Benefit Settlement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Employee separation due to authorized causes (retrenchment, redundancy, closure, installation of labor-saving devices) requiring separation pay under Article 298–299 of the Labor Code; or employee retirement under company retirement plan or RA 7641; or settlement of retirement benefit upon resignation/termination
Frequency: ~20–40 separation pay events/year (mostly retrenchment/redundancy); ~30–50 retirement benefit settlements/year
Volume: ~50–90 events/year
Owner: HR Manager
Participants: HR Manager, HR Specialist, Payroll Officer, Legal, Finance Manager, Controller, DOLE (for retrenchment), Employee
Source: workflow W1385 — Employee Separation Pay Computation, DOLE Clearance &amp; Retirement Benefit Settlement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1385_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1385_Lane1" name="HR Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1385_Lane2" name="HR Specialist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1385_Lane3" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1385_Lane4" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1385_Lane5" name="Payroll Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1385_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1385_Start7" name="Employee separation due to authorized causes (retrenchment, redundancy, closure…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task8" name="Trigger identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Trigger identification: HR Manager identifies separation type — (a) Retrenchment/Redundancy: HR initiates per W1324 (Labor Code Art. 298–299 compliance); separation pay = ½ month pay × years of service (a fraction of at least 6 months = 1 whole year); (b) Authorized closure: separation pay = 1 month pay × years of service; (c) Retirement: employee reaches retirement age (company plan age or RA 7641 age 65); separation pay computed per company retirement plan formula (W977); (d) Just cause termination: no separation pay required (but employee entitled to final pay and 13th month proration per W1383/W1384)
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task9" name="Separation pay computation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Separation pay computation: HR Specialist computes using payroll/HRIS data: (a) Monthly pay rate: basic monthly salary at time of separation; (b) Years of service: from hire date to last working day (inclusive of probationary period); (c) Separation pay formula: ½ month pay per year of service (retrenchment) or 1 month pay per year of service (closure/retirement); (d) &quot;Month pay&quot; definition: per DOLE, &quot;½ month pay&quot; = ½ × (basic monthly salary + 1/12 of 13th month pay + 1/12 of cash equivalent of SIL); commonly simplified to 15 days + 2.5 days (1/12 of 13th month) + 1.25 days (1/12 of SIL) = ½ month pay = ~18.75 days per year of service; (e) compute total separation pay; (f) check tax exemption: separation pay due to death, sickness, or authorized cause is exempt from tax per NIRC Section 32(B)(6)(b); (g) for retirement pay: exempt if retirement plan is approved by BIR and employee is at least 50 years old with 10+ years of service
Responsible (R): HR Specialist
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 30 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task10" name="Legal review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Legal review (for retrenchment/redundancy): Legal reviews separation pay computation and ensures compliance with DOLE DO 174 requirements — (a) 30-day advance notice to employee and DOLE; (b) separation pay computation correctness; (c) retrenchment justification documentation; (d) DOLE Regional Office notification filed
Responsible (R): Legal
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 1 hour/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task11" name="DOLE clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DOLE clearance (for retrenchment/redundancy affecting 50+ employees): HR Manager files retrenchment notice with DOLE Regional Office at least 30 days before effectivity; includes list of affected employees, positions, length of service, separation pay computation, and justification; DOLE may schedule a conference to verify compliance
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): Legal
Duration: 4–8 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task12" name="Approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Approval: CHRO approves separation pay computation; Finance Manager verifies computation; Controller approves GL posting; for amounts &gt; PHP 500,000 per employee or total &gt; PHP 5M: CFO approval required
Responsible (R): CHRO / Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 15 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task13" name="Payment processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Payment processing: Payroll Officer processes separation pay as off-cycle payment — (a) if tax-exempt: gross amount released in full (no withholding); (b) if partially taxable (e.g., separation pay exceeding tax-exempt limit): withhold tax on excess per NIRC graduated rates; (c) system posts: Dr. Separation Pay Expense / Cr. Cash; Dr. Separation Pay Expense / Cr. Withholding Tax Payable (if taxable)
Responsible (R): Payroll Officer
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 10 min/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task14" name="Retirement benefit settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Retirement benefit settlement (for retiring employees): (a) HR Specialist computes retirement benefit per company plan (W977) — compare company plan benefit vs. RA 7641 minimum; apply higher amount; (b) coordinate with retirement fund trustee for fund withdrawal; (c) Payroll processes retirement benefit payment; (d) for BIR-approved retirement plan: benefit is tax-exempt per NIRC; (e) issue Certificate of Employment with retirement notation
Responsible (R): HR Specialist / Payroll
Accountable (A): HR Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/employee</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1385_Task15" name="Quarterly">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly: HR Manager reports separation pay and retirement benefit costs to Finance for accrual tracking and budget variance analysis
Responsible (R): HR Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 30 min/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1385_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1385_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1385_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1385_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-300 (ensure controlled execution — Separation &amp; Benefits (PA-19.5).) | - operational: HR Manager review and approval gate
Owner: HR Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
